fieldsmith 1
# === FIELDSMITH LITERATE CASE ===
# @id: A9
# @code: A9
# @category: analytic
# @level: Analytic Verification
# @title: Analytic Benchmark A9: Certified Dual Prager–Synge / Fenchel Compliance Bounds C_h ≤ C_true ≤ C(σ*) (V34 / V35)
# @subtitle: Verify Galerkin primal compliance lower bound C_h = fᵀ u_h ≤ C_true (V34) and H(div)-equilibrated quadratic stress recovery upper bound C(σ*) (V35) on in-span uniaxial tension and off-span cubic manufactured fields.
# @verification_badge: Verified by V34 & V35 · Certified Primal–Dual Energy Bracket · PASS (0.001%)
# @doc_path: docs/analytic-tests/A9-dual-compliance-bounds-prager-synge.md
# @fsm_path: examples/analytic/A9-dual-compliance-bounds-prager-synge.fsm
# @starter_fsm_name: a9-dual-compliance-bounds.fsm
# @verification_refs: docs/verification/V34.md, docs/verification/V35.md
# ---
# @check: In-Span Uniaxial Tension Primal Lower Bound C_h & Dual Upper Bound C(σ*) || C_true = F² L / (E A) = c² V / E   (40×10×10 mm bar, F = 10 N, E = 1500 MPa) || 0.02666667 N·mm (Pipeline) / 0.4000000 N·mm (T1) || 0.02666667 N·mm / 0.4000000 N·mm || 0.000% || ≤ 0.0001%
# @check: Off-Span Cubic Field (T2) Primal Lower Bound C_h ≤ C_true (24 → 192 tets) || C_true − C_h = a(u* − u_h, u* − u_h) ≥ 0   (Strict Galerkin Orthogonality) || 18,432.00 N·mm || 18,430.86 → 18,431.93 N·mm || 0.006% → 0.0004% || C_h ≤ C_true
# @check: Off-Span Cubic Field (T2) Equilibrated Stress Certificate C(σ*) & Witnesses || J(σ*) = ∫ σ* : S : σ* dV  s.t.  div σ* + b = 0,  ⟦σ* n⟧ = 0,  σ* n|_ΓN = t̄ || 18,432.00 N·mm (Witnesses = 0 N) || 18,431.99 N·mm (Equil 1.04×10⁻⁸ N) || 0.00003% || ≤ 0.01%
# ---
# @assert: Exact Primal Compliance C_h = F² L / (E A) || compliance || 0.0266667 || 0.5% || N·mm
# @assert: Uniaxial Tensile Stress σ_xx = F / A || max_vm_elem || 0.1000 || 0.5% || MPa
# @assert: Tip Axial Extension u_x(L) || max_displacement || 0.0026667 || 5.0% || mm
# ---
# @step: 1. Inspect the Pure-Tension Bar with Exact Kinematic Supports in Setup (2) || setup
#   Open Setup (2). A 40 × 10 × 10 mm bar (A = 100 mm², V = 4,000 mm³, E = 1,500 MPa) is supported by single-component rollers on x = 0, y = 0, z = 0 and pulled by F_x = 10 N on x = 40 mm (traction c = 0.1 MPa).
# @expected:
#   The exact displacement u* = (c/E)(x, −νy, −νz) lies inside the P2 span, so both primal and dual compliance bounds collapse onto the exact energy.
# @step: 2. Verify Exact Compliance C = F² L / (E A) = 0.026667 N·mm and Peak u_x = 0.002667 mm in Results (3) || results
#   Switch to Results (3). The exact work of the external load is C_true = F u_x(L) = 10 × (0.1 × 40 / 1500) = 0.02666667 N·mm. Fieldsmith reports CaseResult.compliance = 0.02666667 N·mm and peak displacement 0.00266667 mm (0.000% error).
# @expected:
#   Displacement is linear in X and compliance equals 0.02667 N·mm.
# ---
# @theory_title: Analytic Verification A9 — Prager–Synge Hypercircle & Fenchel Dual Compliance Certificates (V34 / V35)
# @theory_summary:
#   Proves that P2 Galerkin finite elements provide a guaranteed lower bound C_h ≤ C_true on structural compliance, while H(div)-equilibrated piecewise-quadratic stress recovery provides the complementary Fenchel certificate.
# @theory_section: A9.1 Galerkin Orthogonality Lower Bound & H(div) Equilibrated Recovery
# @theory_eq:
#   a(u* − u_h, v_h) = 0  ∀ v_h ∈ V_h   ⇒   C_true − C_h = a(u* − u_h, u* − u_h) ≥ 0
#   C(σ*) = ∫_Ω σ* : S : σ* dV,   with  div σ* + b = 0,  ⟦σ* n⟧_F = 0,  σ* n|_{Γ_N} = t̄
# @theory_body:
#   Together, C_h and C(σ*) bracket the true continuum compliance and measure discretization error without requiring an analytic solution.
# ---
# @mcp: Solve Dual Compliance Benchmark via API || solve || {"kind":"solve","dofs":25000}
#   Run the P2 solver on A9 and verify compliance and peak displacement.
# === END LITERATE HEADER ===

name "A9 — Certified Dual Compliance Bounds (V34 / V35)"
custommaterial ref_iso name="Pinned Isotropic Reference (E=1500 MPa, nu=0.30)" e=1500 nu=0.30 a=1.0e-5 yield=50 density=1.2
material ref_iso

box bar size=(40, 10, 10) at=(0, 0, 0)
region x0 = bar.nx
region x1 = bar.px
region y0 = bar.ny
region z0 = bar.nz

support sx x0 fixed=x
support sy y0 fixed=y
support sz z0 fixed=z
load pull x1 force=(10, 0, 0)
solve
